# Workspace Color Identity — Do Not Modify

`peacock.color` and `workbench.colorCustomizations` inside any `.code-workspace` file (e.g. `worktree-1.code-workspace`) are **deliberate workspace identity markers**. They make each git worktree window immediately distinguishable when multiple Cursor windows are open side-by-side.

## ✅ DO

- Leave `peacock.color` and `workbench.colorCustomizations` exactly as-is when they are not the direct subject of the task.
- Preserve **all sub-keys**: `titleBar.activeBackground`, `titleBar.activeForeground`, `titleBar.inactiveBackground`, `titleBar.inactiveForeground`, `titleBar.border`.

## ❌ DO NOT

- Remove, strip, or omit `peacock.color` or `workbench.colorCustomizations` (or any sub-keys) from any `.code-workspace` file.
- Treat these appearance settings as non-essential, clutter, or dead code.
- "Clean up" or "simplify" a `.code-workspace` file by dropping color configuration without explicit developer instruction.

